{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Do You Know What a Gantt Chart Is?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to describe Gantt charts."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common activities at work by using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Interpret the requirements report to determine the technological needs in managing information, based on rules and protocols established by the company."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Participates in simple conversations or simulated situations about the communicative topics for this level through grammar and vocabulary structures."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Recognizes simple ideas on requirement reports, tools for Object Oriented Programming, and other basic programming tools."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more information about Gantt charts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a simple project with a specific outcome to establish the tasks."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a Gantt chart in a poster showing tasks for a month. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Show your final product to your partners and instructor. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search more information about Gantt charts. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I list some tasks for a month. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a poster with a Gantt chart with tasks for a month. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I show my poster and explain it to my partners and instructor."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present Vs. Simple Past with Regular and Irregular Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use the <b>simple past</b> to talk about actions that happened and finished at some point in the past; and the<b> simple present</b> to talk about actions that are generally true or that occur at the present moment.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<b><center>SIMPLE PRESENT</center></b>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use the simple present to talk about general truths or how something usually takes place. Regular verbs in <b>simple present</b> change their form when referring to the third person singular."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>No third person singular  </b>            \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Third person singular</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"eat\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"eats\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"talk\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"talks\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"transfer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"transfers\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are some irregular verbs in simple present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<center>Have/Has </b>Is/Am/Are</b> Do/Does </br>Go/Goes</center>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<center><b>SIMPLE PAST</center></b>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We form the <b>simple past</b> in affirmative sentences by adding \u2018-ed' at the end if the verb is regular. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:</br><i>Last week the analyst <b>sorted</b> the requirements.</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Most verbs in <b>simple past</b> are regular. But there is a considerable number, especially among those verbs we use more frequently, that do not form their simple past tense by adding \u2018-ed' at the end of the verb. Even though there are some regular patters for forming some <b>irregular verbs</b>, you have to learn many of them by heart.  "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Simple Present  </b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Simple Past</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Do\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Did\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Go\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Went\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Drive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Drove\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Run\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Ran\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<center><b>CONTRAST</b></center>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We can use <b>simple present</b> and <b>simple past</b> to make a <b>contrast</b> between how something was or occurred in the past and how that is or takes place now. When we want to contrast the two tenses, we are usually going to use time expressions to indicate at what time each action takes place. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: </br><i>We <b>worked</b> with a very basic software <b>last year</b>, <b>now </b>we <b>use</b> a more advanced version and we are doing much better. </br>We<b> didn't use</b> Gantt charts <b>before</b>,<b> now</b> we <b>organize</b> different tasks much faster by using them. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In the chart below there are some common irregular verbs.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<center><b>Common irregular verbs</b></center>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":12,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Present</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Past</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"say\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"said\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"make\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"made\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"go\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"went\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"take\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"took\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"come\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"came\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"see\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"saw\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"know\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"knew\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"get\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"got\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"give\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"gave\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"find\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"found\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"think\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thought\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "In the past, Gantt charts only summarized the elements of a project, modern charts also show the expected time for a task to finish."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Nowadays Gantt charts are a common charting technique, but when they first appeared, they were considered revolutionary."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The Gantt chart was actually designed by the polish economist Karol Adamiecki in 1896."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Types of Charts: Comparison/Relationship Charts"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <b>charts</b> to communicate and express data clearly."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Gantt charts consist of a bar chart expressing the work break down structure of a project. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You choose a specific type of chart depending on the kind of information you want to show, and how you want to show it. There are charts to state comparison relationships, flow/process, or location."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">Comparison relationships: </span>You use this type of charts to contrast two or more variables. Some of the most common charts used in comparison are line graphs, bar charts, and Venn diagrams."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">Flow / process: </span>You use flow charts to show the development of a process."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">Location:</span> You can, naturally, show location with location charts. "}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob07img01.jpg"}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob07img02.jpg"}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob07img03.jpg"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "seem "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to look like "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Are you working on a project, but you seem to have problems planning and organizing your work?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "deadline "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the final chance to deliver a piece of work"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can use Gantt charts to organize the tasks for a project's schedule, they include the starting point and the deadline of the tasks."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "achieve "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to reach or to obtain something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A Gantt chart organizes every single task required to achieve the goal of a project in a diagram."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "due time "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the designated date to present or deliver a piece of work or to complete a task"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In the past, Gantt charts only summarized the elements of a project, while modern charts show the expected time for a task to finish; the optimistic, realistic, and pessimistic due time; the relation among tasks and their progress in percentages."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "accomplish "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to achieve one's goals"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Get your Gantt chart now and accomplish your projects successfully and on time!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "successfully "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to triumph achieving a goal"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adv.)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Get your Gantt chart now and accomplish your projects successfully and on time!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain what a